-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for TwoTorsion
-- (doc/delooping-direct.pdf, Section 2.3, Steps 1-6: Statement T): one entry per
-- declaration, generated from --opened (28 Oct 2026) and read against the
-- note.  Kinds of openings:
--   types and levels: PtMap, PtSec, PtEquiv, Maps.PMO, Over.Unloop, isContr,
--     isProp, isSet, Equiv, isEquiv, Hom (and Zab, intAb: h.1 applied to an
--     integer), HC, STr.Same, SphereAxiom.O2 (the type of FibP.surj2), the
--     fibre types Fib / Triple.F / f0 (projections w.1), M', PtMapLoops.pt0,
--     ptconst, ENat.M (the bipointed type of delta), KZ4 / kz4;
--   the type of the delooping witness: Deloopable, fibO, Triples (on the
--     declarations after dl), SC3, Omega, realise, PtProp.R (eps: the pointed
--     equivalence of the path Omega Y = realise t has type Omega Y ~pt Fib k);
--   index arithmetic: two, three, four, five, NatArith.plus (cor11 in pi-cell;
--     the numerals of Conv's types K three / K five against CrossGen's
--     K (suc two) / K (suc four): eBi-def, conj-bridge, conv-u); isTrunc
--     (Omega^3 K(B,5) is a 2-type, phi-refl);
--   by-definition steps of the text: ptcomp, fpr (pi at eps^-1 v, pi-sec);
--     pi, fk, Ghat, f', a, tgt, xA, gamma', phi (the local definitions);
--     Lev.conj, Lev.eBi (Ghat is conj two (K(a,2)), ghat-loop); Inv.lam
--     (lambda_g m = loop^2 m g, phi-pi, lam-fp); pt-inv / Acc.inv (the
--     inverse of e_2 is the sec of its equivalence, phi-refl, as
--     CrossGen.cell-of); EDelta.e2i, Inv.dfun, CrossGen.Cj-fun, Dp, Maps.D
--     (h-cell: Cj, D and Delta by definition, as Cross.diag-null); Conj.eBi,
--     Conj.conj (conj-bridge); Phi, Conv.F (eh-cls); hcl (two-tors: the
--     classes are the inc of STr);
--   extras, not steps of the text: the chain KZ2 -> KK.K -> EMSpace.K ->
--     EMn.Kstage / stage2 -> EM2.K2 -> Deloop.Torsors.Tor opened for variables
--     over KZ2 and the aliases KZ2 / kz2 (the etaV mechanism,
--     doc/etav-lock-diagnostic.txt).
-- eps is locked after its definition (only its type is used; pi-sec opened
-- its construction PtProp.I.equiv before).
